# require_cc_guard.z -- the C backend knows what quadfloat needs of the C
# compiler (natives.tbl's `@unit.system.quadfloat` row), so asking for tcc
# reports the unit, the feature and the compiler by name instead of letting
# tcc reject the emitted C. The flag rides in on the .zcargs sidecar; no C
# compiler is invoked on this path, so tcc need not be installed for this to
# pass.
main: function is {
    x: 1.5.f128
    print "\{x}"
}
